.TH WORCESTERSHIRE 1 "2026" "Worcestershire 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
worcestershire \- high-performance wordlist generator
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B worcestershire
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B worcestershire
generates wordlists by applying one or more transformation strategies
(combination types) to a set of input words.
Output is streamed directly to disk so memory usage remains constant
regardless of the size of the resulting wordlist.
.PP
When invoked without arguments the interactive setup wizard is launched.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.
.SS Input
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-words " " \fIWORDS\fR
Space-separated list of words to process.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-input " " \fIFILE\fR
Read input words from \fIFILE\fR, one word per line.
May be specified multiple times to load from several files.
.
.SS Output
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Write output to \fIFILE\fR.
Default: \fBoutput.lst\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-format " " \fIFMT\fR
Output format.
.RS
.IP \fBtxt\fR
One word per line (default).
.IP \fBjson\fR
One JSON object per line: \fB{"word":"value"}\fR.
.IP \fBhashcat\fR
One word per line, compatible with hashcat wordlist input.
.RE
.TP
.B \-\-compress
Compress the output file with gzip.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Overwrite the output file without prompting.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Estimate the number of combinations that would be generated and exit
without writing any output.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress all non-essential output (progress bar, summary).
.
.SS Combination types
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-combination " " \fICOMBOS\fR
Space-separated list of combination type numbers to apply (1\(en8).
See
.B COMBINATION TYPES
below.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-depth " " \fIDEPTH\fR
Maximum number of words to mix together for combination type 1 (Word Mix).
Accepted range: 2\(en5.
Default: \fB3\fR.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-min " " \fIMIN\fR
Discard output words shorter than \fIMIN\fR characters.
Default: \fB0\fR.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-max " " \fIMAX\fR
Discard output words longer than \fIMAX\fR characters.
Default: \fB20\fR.
.
.SS Encoding and hashing
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-encode " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Encode or hash every output word before writing.
Available formats:
.BR base64 ", " base32 ", " url ", " hex ", " md5 ", " sha1 ", " sha256 ", " sha512 .
.
.SS Advanced
.TP
.B \-\-max\-combinations " " \fIN\fR
Stop after generating \fIN\fR combinations.
.TP
.B \-\-rules " " \fIFILE\fR
Apply a JTR-style rule file.
Each line is one rule; a rule is a sequence of single-character commands
applied left to right to each word.
Supported commands: \fBl\fR (lowercase), \fBu\fR (uppercase),
\fBc\fR (capitalise), \fBr\fR (reverse), \fBd\fR (duplicate),
\fB$\fR (append !), \fB^\fR (prepend !).
.TP
.B \-\-resume " " \fIFILE\fR
Resume a previously interrupted run.
\fIFILE\fR is a JSON state file written by an earlier run.
.TP
.B \-\-log\-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Append log messages to \fIFILE\fR instead of stdout.
.TP
.B \-\-log\-level " " \fILEVEL\fR
Minimum log level to emit.
One of \fBdebug\fR, \fBinfo\fR, \fBwarn\fR, \fBerror\fR.
Default: \fBinfo\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-buffer\-size " " \fIBYTES\fR
Output buffer size in bytes.
Default: \fB1048576\fR (1 MiB).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI colour codes in terminal output.
.TP
.B \-\-parallel
Enable multi-threaded generation.
Requires the program to be compiled with \fB\-Dpreview_mt\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-workers " " \fIN\fR
Number of concurrent worker fibers when \fB\-\-parallel\fR is active.
Default: \fB4\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-cache\-size " " \fIN\fR
Size of the LRU cache used to memoize encoding results.
Default: \fB1000\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-max\-memory " " \fIBYTES\fR
Abort if heap usage exceeds \fIBYTES\fR bytes.
.
.SS Custom dictionaries
.TP
.B \-\-homograph\-dict " " \fIFILE\fR
Override the built-in homograph substitution table.
.TP
.B \-\-leet\-dict " " \fIFILE\fR
Override the built-in leet substitution table.
.TP
.B \-\-salt\-dict " " \fIFILE\fR
Override the built-in salt dictionary.
.TP
.B \-\-affix\-dict " " \fIFILE\fR
Override the built-in affix dictionary.
.
.SS Configuration
.TP
.B \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Load options from a YAML configuration file.
Command-line flags take precedence over file values.
See
.B CONFIGURATION FILE
below for the supported keys.
.
.SS Informational
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
Print all combination types with their numbers and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-preset " " \fINAME\fR
Apply a named preset before processing other options.
Available presets:
.BR password\-cracking ", " username\-enum ", " quick\-test .
.TP
.B \-\-suggest
Analyse the input words and print a suggested set of combination types, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-verbose
Print additional diagnostic messages during generation.
.TP
.BR \-N ", " \-\-noprogress
Disable the progress bar.
.TP
.B \-\-examples
Print usage examples and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-explain " " \fICOMBOS\fR
Print a description of the specified combination types and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-interactive
Launch the interactive setup wizard.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version string and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a help summary and exit.
.
.SH COMBINATION TYPES
.TP
.B 1 \ Word Mix
Concatenates permutations of the input words at depths 2 through
.I DEPTH
(see \fB\-d\fR).
For two words \fIpass\fR and \fIword\fR at depth 2 this produces
\fIpassword\fR and \fIwordpass\fR.
.TP
.B 2 \ Case Alternate
Generates every possible upper/lower case variant of each word.
For words longer than 10 characters only three variants are generated
(lowercase, uppercase, capitalised) to avoid combinatorial explosion.
.TP
.B 3 \ Homograph
Substitutes characters with visually similar alternatives drawn from the
homograph dictionary.
For example: \fIa\fR becomes \fI@\fR, \fI4\fR, \fI\[*a]\fR, or a Cyrillic
look-alike.
.TP
.B 4 \ Reverser
Reverses each word character by character.
.TP
.B 5 \ Saltify
Prepends and appends each entry in the salt dictionary to each word.
.TP
.B 6 \ Leet Speak
Substitutes characters with common leet equivalents
(\fIe\fR\(->3, \fIs\fR\(->5, \fIo\fR\(->0, etc.).
.TP
.B 7 \ Separator Insert
Joins pairs and triples of input words with separator characters
(\fI\-\fR, \fI_\fR, \fI.\fR, \fI+\fR, \fI@\fR, and the empty string).
.TP
.B 8 \ Affix
Prepends and appends entries from the affix dictionary to each word.
.
.SH CONFIGURATION FILE
A YAML file passed via \fB\-\-config\fR may contain the following keys.
All values are optional; any that are absent are left at their defaults
or taken from the command line.
.PP
.nf
depth:            integer (2-5)
min_length:       integer (0-49)
max_length:       integer (1-50)
format:           string  (txt | json | hashcat)
compress:         boolean
max_combinations: integer
buffer_size:      integer
workers:          integer
cache_size:       integer
max_memory:       integer
combinations:
  - integer
  - integer
.fi
.
.SH PRESETS
Presets apply a pre-defined configuration tuned for a specific use case.
Command-line flags override preset values.
.TP
.B password\-cracking
All combination types, depth 4, length 8\(en32, compressed txt output,
10\|000\|000 combination limit.
.TP
.B username\-enum
Combination types 2, 4, 7, depth 2, length 4\(en20, plain txt output,
1\|000\|000 combination limit.
.TP
.B quick\-test
Combination types 1 and 2, depth 2, base64 encoding, JSON output,
1\|000 combination limit.
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred (bad option, missing file, encoding error, memory limit exceeded, etc.).
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I output.lst
Default output file when \fB\-o\fR is not specified.
.TP
.I state.json
Conventional name for a resume state file (any path may be used).
.
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate a wordlist from two words using Word Mix and Case Alternate:
.PP
.RS
.nf
worcestershire \-w "password admin" \-c 1 2 \-o wordlist.txt
.fi
.RE
.PP
Process a file with all combination types and compress the output:
.PP
.RS
.nf
worcestershire \-i base.txt \-c 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 \-\-compress \-o full.lst.gz
.fi
.RE
.PP
Hash every output word with SHA256:
.PP
.RS
.nf
worcestershire \-i words.txt \-e sha256 \-o hashes.txt
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use the password-cracking preset:
.PP
.RS
.nf
worcestershire \-i words.txt \-\-preset password\-cracking \-o cracking.lst
.fi
.RE
.PP
Estimate output size without writing:
.PP
.RS
.nf
worcestershire \-i words.txt \-c 1 2 3 \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
.PP
Resume an interrupted run:
.PP
.RS
.nf
worcestershire \-i words.txt \-c 1 2 \-o out.lst \-\-resume state.json \-\-force
.fi
.RE
.
